d 'NEARMRG': module to nearest match merging of two datasets on a numeric variable
d
d  nearmrg merges a using dataset onto the data in memory by
d NEAREST value of a numeric variable rather than by exact
d equality, which is what you want when the keys are dates,
d timestamps, or measurements that differ by rounding. For every
d master observation it finds the closest value of nearvar() in the
d using file, optionally within exact matches of a varlist, and
d optionally restricted to values at or below (lower) or at or
d above (upper) the master value. A limit() caps how far a match
d may reach; distance() records how far it did. Master and using
d variables may carry different names, and all standard merge
d options (keepusing, update, replace) pass through. Original
d package co-authored by Michael Blasnik and Katherine Smith
d (2003); taken over and rewritten by Eric A. Booth beginning in
d 2010. 
d
d KW: merge; data management; nearest neighbour; panel data
d
d Requires: Stata version 11.0
d
d Distribution-Date: 20260730
d
d Author: Eric A. Booth, Texas 2036
d Support: email eric.a.booth@@gmail.com
d
f nearmrg.ado
f nearmrg.sthlp
